"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative focused on enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a budget of $2M approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase and the testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing. The project is currently moving into the development phase, with lead developer Omar Jensen providing guidance. Future plans include user interface enhancements starting in October, security protocol updates (including multi-factor authentication) effective January next year, and ongoing feedback collection from stakeholders. Additionally, the team is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology. A bug report was also received regarding a specific character issue in the system."
